      },
      "text": "Cancer pharmacology kills tumor cells by exploiting differences between tumor and normal cells — a progressively smaller differential the more targeted the therapy. Traditional chemotherapy exploits rapid proliferation; targeted therapy exploits specific oncogenic mutations; immunotherapy activates the immune system."
